# The affiant-protocol ref this repository's conformance driver is pinned to.
#
# Versions of the rulebook (https://github.com/Sakwala/affiant-protocol) are git tags.
# The pin is the v0.1.2 tag, and `commit` records what that tag points at, so a reader
# can check one against the other with no network. While a version's text is on the
# rulebook's default branch and its tag has not been cut, `tag` is empty and the COMMIT
# is the pin: a commit is as immutable as a tag and, unlike a tag, cannot be moved
# under a running build.
#
# Changing this file is a reviewable diff in this repository's own history: a format
# change arrives as a pull request, never as a silent upstream shift under a build.
#
# `conformance/sync.sh` reads this file. `conformance/sync.sh --verify` re-checks the
# vendored copy under tests/Affiant.Conformance.Tests/protocol/ against SHA256SUMS,
# which is what CI runs, so a local edit to a vendored fixture cannot pass unnoticed.

repository=https://github.com/Sakwala/affiant-protocol
commit=d803fb0740c4b86dd6560c8614d7eb9e47b5b333
tag=v0.1.2
tag_note=v0.1.2 was cut on the commit above on 2026-09-05: SR-1 now states that the canonical form is taken over the Affidavit as the schema defines it, protocolVersion included; the two conformance fixtures that pin a content hash (sequence-a/approve-round-trip, decide/amend-recompute) carry hashes regenerated from the corrected reference, because the ones published at v0.1.1 came from a runtime whose model did not carry that property and so disagreed with the schema and with all seven canonical byte vectors; and GT-4 now states the entry-id derivation - the tenant, the conversation, the tool and the canonical form of the operation and its arguments, digested and laid out as a version-8 UUID - which was previously left to an implementation and is inside every content hash through a reviewer-act binding. The 0.1.0 wire schemas are unchanged.
vendored=tests/Affiant.Conformance.Tests/protocol
